  Carry the settled model through API/view models in that
  follow-on; no server or web file is owned here.
- **Filed provenance rendering:** W-087's filed date/by row from item events;
  distinguish snapshot observation from an actual filing date. No fabricated
  historical author/date and no new filing metadata in W-096.
- **Inbox work-kind context:** future API and display work; do not confuse
  opus kind with write-result kind or petitio subject/body.
- **Dependency scheduling (W-068):** depends/blocks, ordering and readiness
  dependencies. Also excluded: rank, amendment-history display, arc progress
  roll-ups, filters, grouping, sorting, drag/drop and planned dates.
- **Delegation migration (D-029):** tier removal and munus-to-seat records/UI.
  No change to the existing munera enumeration or seat model ownership.
- No wire attribute renaming, lifecycle state additions/renaming, new
  probatio status enums, Jira import/synchronization, new QA gate, automatic
  reinterpretation of old `opus` work as `ui`, or historical evidence backfill.
- No spec gate signature and no edit to `studio/opera/W-096.md` in this draft.

## Petitio candidates

None required to draft this bounded model. “Routes review to ui-lead” is
interpreted under D-022 as required design/red-team input which the censor
cites and disposes of, regardless of its recommendation. The censor remains
the single review/QA gate; no ui-lead-signed gate is introduced. Start/end
are actual transition dates, consistent
with the opus title, not scheduling estimates. These choices are explicit for
the unsigned spec's review; neither quietly amends the Patron's authority.

